{
  "name": "Pendulum Wave",
  "notes": "Five pendulums at 0.100, 0.104, 0.108, 0.112 and 0.116 Hz. They start together, spread into a travelling wave, pass through a phase where they alternate, briefly look random, and re-converge -- and the full cycle is the reciprocal of the 0.004 Hz difference, about four minutes. Nothing sequences any of that. It is five sines and arithmetic, which is exactly why the real desk toy is mesmerising.\n\nThe ratio is the whole design. Equal rates would be one fat line; a wide spread would be five unrelated blinkers. It has to be a small CONSTANT difference, which is why the Speed knob drives all five through rows at identical depth -- adding the same amount to each preserves the difference and therefore the four-minute cycle, where a multiplicative knob would not.\n\nThe `tile` on the trail layer is the shadow of the whole ensemble repeated, and its count is on the same slow source as the mirror centre beneath, so the ghosts crowd together as the bobs converge. The chain is `M5 -> M0.rate` on the slowest pendulum ALONE, which detunes the arithmetic slightly and means the re-convergence is never quite exact -- a real cradle has friction and never repeats either. Ultraviolet run across the five bobs, one hue each, 252 to 300 degrees, with the trail on the sodium accent so the ghosts read warm behind cold bobs.",
